To change the default bridge network IP range, you can use the `--bip` flag with the `dockerd` command [Source 9]. The `--bip` flag is used to specify the IPv4 address for the default bridge [Source 9].

Here's an example of how to use the `--bip` flag:

```console
$ sudo dockerd --bip 192.168.1.0/24
```

This will set the default bridge network IP range to `192.168.1.0/24` [Source 9].

Alternatively, you can also specify the default bridge network IP range in the `daemon.json` file by adding the `bip` key with the desired IP range [Source 5].

Here's an example of how to specify the default bridge network IP range in the `daemon.json` file:

```json
{
  "default-network-opts": {
    "bridge": {
      "com.docker.network.bridge.bip": "192.168.1.0/24"
    }
  }
}
```

This will also set the default bridge network IP range to `192.168.1.0/24` [Source 5].

Note that changing the default bridge network IP range will not affect pre-existing networks [Source 3].
